#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151901 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63580eb-b476-51fa-a005-560f6e57d911" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Point Under a Linear Transformation of a Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "d2dafa69-6a9b-5f99-a16d-5fe5529ffd66" :question/math-academy-id "e-6704" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point $B',$ the image of $B(2,-3)$ under the action of $\\mathbf T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $B$ under the action of $\\mathbf T,$ we first create a column vector $\\mathbf{x}$ containing the coordinates of $B{:}$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $\\mathbf{x}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $T\\mathbf{x}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $T \\mathbf{x},$ contains the coordinates of $B'.$ Therefore, $B'(3,-5).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151902 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/id #uuid "2195a964-074f-5beb-abcd-ba0229e2872b" :question/math-academy-id "e-6705" :question/problem "Consider the line $5x-y-3=0$ and linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $\\mathbf T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find two points on the given line. Solving for $y,$ we get $y=5x-3,$ and substituting $x=0$ and $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0\\, & \\to \\,y=5(0)-3=-3, \\\\ x=1\\, & \\to \\,y=5(1)-3=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have two points on the line, $P(0,-3)$ and $Q(1,2).$\n\nTo find the images of $P$ and $Q$ under the action of $\\mathbf T,$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of $P$ and $Q$ in its columns:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are $P'(-3,-6)$ and $Q'(-1,3).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through $P'$ and $Q'\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-6) & =\\frac{3-(-6)}{-1-(-3)}(x-(-3)) \\\\ y+6 & =\\frac{9}{2}(x+3) \\\\ 2y+12 & =9x+27 \\\\ 9x-2y+15 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151903 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c8f0fa1-a86a-577f-bdc9-fc7427faa18d" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Slope-Intercept Form"}] :question/id #uuid "2192176c-e983-5913-b159-4d2bffd72ae1" :question/math-academy-id "e-6713" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=3x-2$ and linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $\\mathbf T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's find two points on the given line. Substituting $x=0$ and $x=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0\\, & \\to \\,y=3(0)-2=-2, \\\\ x=1\\, & \\to \\,y=3(1)-2=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have two points on the line, $P(0,-2)$ and $Q(1,1).$\n\nTo find the images of $P$ and $Q$ under the action of $\\mathbf T,$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of $P$ and $Q$ in its columns:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are $P'(0,-2)$ and $Q'(-1,4).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through $P'$ and $Q'\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-2) & =\\frac{4-(-2)}{-1-0}(x-0) \\\\ y+2 & =-6x \\\\ 6x+y+2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280928 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a4390ea-6347-5152-885b-ce7f60e0b73c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-17y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280930}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a4390ea-6347-5152-885b-ce7f60e0b73c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-17y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280930} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9634137-e64d-5b61-a9e1-5d0760d323e9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "809b9f25-344f-56b6-953a-27ba29139b9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-275719" :question/problem "Consider the line $4x-y-3=0$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=27.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $4x-y-3=0$ passes through the points $U(0,-3)$ and $V(1,1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $U$ and $V$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 & 5 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${U}^{′}(-12,-3)$ and ${V}^{′}(5,-1).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-3) & =\\frac{-1-(-3)}{5-(-12)}(x-(-12)) \\\\ y+3 & =\\frac{2}{17}(x+12)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+3 & =\\frac{2}{17}(x+12) \\\\ 17y+51 & =2x+24 \\\\ 51-24 & =2x-17y \\\\ 2x-17y & =27\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280942 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c8f0fa1-a86a-577f-bdc9-fc7427faa18d" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Slope-Intercept Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab2cc4f3-7790-5ea8-84ac-826e6fcb166e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7x+10y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab2cc4f3-7790-5ea8-84ac-826e6fcb166e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7x+10y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280944} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d280eba-bd43-5257-80cf-1cea230f9f70" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8680e675-b4fd-563b-ae15-e54ded036ebe" :question/math-academy-id "q-281130" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=-\\frac{2}{3}x-3$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=-81.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=-\\frac{2}{3}x-3$ passes through the points $A(0,-3)$ and $B(3,-5)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 7 \\\\ -6 & -13\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(-3,-6)$ and ${B}^{′}(7,-13).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+6 & =\\frac{-13+6}{7-(-3)}(x+3) \\\\ y+6 & =-\\frac{7}{10}(x+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10y+60 & =-7x-21 \\\\ 7x+10y & =-81\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c6784ba-0bcf-5132-b031-9ca99c91e25b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x+5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c6784ba-0bcf-5132-b031-9ca99c91e25b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x+5y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280951} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdbd96d5-67fa-52eb-9b72-b1a6da45dacd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "91f5a824-ec1d-58a0-a686-86bca0afba26" :question/math-academy-id "q-281583" :question/problem "Consider the line $3x+2y-6=0$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=42.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $3x+2y-6=0$ passes through the points $P(0,3)$ and $Q(2,0)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $P$ and $Q$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 4 \\\\ -6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${P}^{′}(9,-6)$ and ${Q}^{′}(4,2).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${P}^{′}$ and ${Q}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-6) & =\\frac{2-(-6)}{4-9}(x-9) \\\\ y+6 & =\\frac{8}{-5}(x-9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+6 & =-\\frac{8}{5}(x-9) \\\\ 5y+30 & =-8x+72 \\\\ 8x+5y & =42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n8x+5y=42\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63580eb-b476-51fa-a005-560f6e57d911" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Point Under a Linear Transformation of a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8251953a-49f4-5d26-b78f-9ba3efd9e7c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151063} {:answer/id #uuid "d2cd5e1b-08d6-58af-b649-3bbf6df34b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151064} {:answer/id #uuid "d7eac83e-4d47-504a-bd45-d040debd9599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0, 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151065} {:answer/id #uuid "d938875d-57fc-5cb2-b2be-7a335a0f8c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1, 0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151066} {:answer/id #uuid "565b989b-4cf7-5c96-badd-cfbcc40aa4a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2, 0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8251953a-49f4-5d26-b78f-9ba3efd9e7c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2, 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151063} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb370210-574f-55b5-a16d-2ada03fa4058" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186151062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dd69ce92-0c38-503f-b13d-fc02108de3ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-77543" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point ${A}^{′}$, the image of $A(-1,1)$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $A$ under the action of $T$, we first create a column-vector $x$ containing the coordinates of $A:$\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $x$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $Tx:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $Tx,$ contains the coordinates of ${A}^{′}.$ Therefore, ${A}^{′}(2,1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280956 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f63580eb-b476-51fa-a005-560f6e57d911" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Point Under a Linear Transformation of a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95de2d9a-d163-5770-a741-02b6d9cd9188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280958} {:answer/id #uuid "111a8184-54d9-5473-aef8-a922b4e99a4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280959} {:answer/id #uuid "14e08eb5-6564-5320-ba3e-800ac3c4ee02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280960} {:answer/id #uuid "e2404d92-199e-5d01-ae9c-ab5eaa74aeb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280961} {:answer/id #uuid "53aa0f3e-1457-5d35-97c9-6c07ca006aba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95de2d9a-d163-5770-a741-02b6d9cd9188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280958} :answer-field/id #uuid "c897eb38-4937-53a7-90a0-2b37762d042c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280957}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d473e2c3-3e9c-577f-941a-1098b72dd4bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-77722" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the coordinates of the point ${F}^{′}$, the image of $F(2,-2)$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $F$ under the action of $T$, we first create a column-vector $x$ containing the coordinates of $F:$\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $x$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $Tx:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Tx & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result, $Tx,$ contains the coordinates of ${F}^{′}.$ Therefore, ${F}^{′}(2,6).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280970 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c8f0fa1-a86a-577f-bdc9-fc7427faa18d" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Slope-Intercept Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc0b484c-2cfd-5a55-ac48-2f380cf6db30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+y-24=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280972} {:answer/id #uuid "bb13ebfe-dea1-5938-91f8-531d04e871bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-y+8=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280973} {:answer/id #uuid "69bf48e6-a1ee-55fa-95a1-6c28604cf206" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+y+24=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280974} {:answer/id #uuid "961c3500-d27e-5d7e-8f61-763a2f32afa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-y+24=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280975} {:answer/id #uuid "b1dcd5a0-96e6-545c-98e6-81fa6a9fa489" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+y-8=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc0b484c-2cfd-5a55-ac48-2f380cf6db30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+y-24=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280972} :answer-field/id #uuid "628a0264-aaab-5f5b-8bdb-30974343600d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e1d4b30-c2f9-5d8e-ac8c-cb94e781f714" :question/math-academy-id "q-77779" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=-x-4$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=-x-4$ passes through the points $W(0,-4)$ and $Z(1,-5)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $W$ and $Z$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${W}^{′}(8,0)$ and ${Z}^{′}(9,-3).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${W}^{′}$ and ${Z}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =\\frac{-3-0}{9-8}(x-8) \\\\ y & =-3(x-8) \\\\ y & =-3x+24 \\\\ 3x+y-24 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
